  "title": "ArtTet & ArtMesh: Reconstructing Articulated Objects with Part-Aware Mesh Fields",
  "summary": "ArtTet reconstructs articulated objects from multi-view observations using a divide-and-conquer strategy, while ArtMesh builds on a mesh-native approach to achieve per-part motion and geometric reconstruction. Both methods use rigid-body rules and dynamic articulation inference to ensure joint types and part labels are preserved without part masks.",
  "facts": [
